Negative control for the editor's SETTLED close.

Closes the editor whichever way the save settles, so a refused save dismisses
the form and takes the user's input with it — leaving the toast as the only
trace of a record that was never persisted.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the form-flow save specs — a rejected save keeps the form on screen.

